// `--prove` and `--lemma` values that name no lemma of the theory.
//
// `checkIfLemmasInTheory` (Theory/Tools/Wellformedness.hs:1156-1171) reports
// them through `findNotProvedLemmas` (Theory/Tools/Wellformedness.hs:1140-1151),
// a `foldl` that prepends each mismatch and so reverses its input.  That input
// is `findArg "prove" as ++ findArg "lemma" as` (Main/TheoryLoader.hs:326) over
// an argument list `addArg` builds by prepending (Main/Console.hs:269-270,279-280),
// so one flag's values arrive reversed.  The two reversals put the `--lemma`
// values first, in command-line order, followed by the `--prove` values.
//
// Mode `match`: the two engines list the four names in the same order.
//
// Compared slice: the wf report block.


theory S8LemmaArgOrder
begin

rule R:
  [ Fr(~x) ] --[ A(~x) ]-> [ Out(~x) ]

lemma real:
  "All x #i. A(x) @ #i ==> T"

end
